[Music]  hi there i'm lucia subari technical lead  for google cloud cortex framework and  today i'd like to deep dive into the  technical details of our cortex data  foundation for sap  from previous videos you know that  google cloud cortex framework delivers  not just the reference architecture to  solve business problems but we also  deliver solution content templates and  deployment accelerators  we provide not just the recipe but we  also include the ingredients and some  pro tips to make your meal as tasty as  possible  let's first take a look at the  ingredients for the cortex data  foundation for sap  we start with raw table data from an sap  cc or s4hana system  we want to land the data into bigquery  and we want to make sure the data is  both consistent and updated as  frequently as our business requires  the records keep changing as updates  deletes and inserts flow into bigquery  this means we need an automated way to  process these records that are  constantly changing such as scripts to  process change data capture or cdc for  short  finally we need to make sure our users  can make sense of the current data  answer business questions and improve  decisions with insights powered by  machine learning  we also want to give users the  flexibility to consume insights with  their preferred reporting tool of choice  an application or even a spreadsheet  so how does google cloud cortex  framework help you put these ingredients  together let's take a deeper look  we want to keep the integrations options  open so any tool that gets the data into  the same structure with the same field  names as in the original sap tables work  if you follow an elt pattern as it's  preferable with bigquery you need a way  to distinguish which is the latest  replicated record for reporting purposes  this is accomplished by loading each  record with a timestamp and an operation  flag  once the raw data records are in  bigquery you have two options to process  the data leveraging the provided cdc  processing scripts  the first one you can generate views to  scan the raw table and pick the latest  record in real time  this is useful when you're replicating  data in near real time from a tool like  our bigquery connector for sap slt and  the business wants updates reflected as  they have  the second option is to use scheduled  jobs in cloud composer to merge or  absert the new or updated record in a  table in a specific frequency in batch  this is a good option to keep costs  under control when the business does not  plan on querying the data in real time  some replication tools have embedded  change data capture processing  capability and merge records directly  when inserting them  in these cases you can skip the cdc  processing in bigquery but we supply the  scripts just in case  now that we have processed our  replicated data and have the latest  changes in bigquery it's time to create  some models  our cortex data foundation has more than  60 pre-built views that anyone can  deploy and adjust to their needs  and the list of modeling objects  available will continue to grow as we  release new content  you will find the current list of views  and the tables they reference in the  entity relationship diagram in the  github repository link below  these views not only incorporate sap  specific business modeling but they also  tackle common but technically hard  challenges to solve such as unit of  measure and currency conversions  and the ability to deploy ecc and s4  models separately of consolidated into a  single view  we will also find scripts to process  data in batches flatten hierarchies and  consume and store data from other  sources such as weather or search trends  through directed acyclic graphs  these scripts are ready to be executed  by cloud composer within a schedule you  can customize according to your business  needs  everything you need to know about the  deployment of our cortex data foundation  is documented in our open source github  repository  you will find the key starting point is  the cloud build file that executes all  of the steps from optionally providing  test data  through generating change data capture  scripts to updates tables with the  latest results to creating the views  that provide the business logics  after you have cloned your repository  you can customize parameters to match  your business needs and available data  sources  and once your cloud build deployment is  complete you will see the data sets you  use test parameters have been populated  and you will find scripts to process  changes and retrieve additional data in  the bucket you have provisioned  these models are foundation to more  advanced solutions for example on the  google cloud marketplace you will find  our cortex application layer content  with sample applications for  synchronously exposing data through rest  apis or integrating with other  applications through pub sub  now that you know what cortex data  foundation is about check out the git  repository link here to deploy the data  foundation solution content you will  find all the step-by-step instructions  there  and this is just the beginning subscribe  to this channel and stay tuned to learn  more about advanced business solutions  and other exacting options like our  microservices-based cortex application  layer  [Music]

